# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in. These are the five values
# that cannot be committed; everything else lives in .env.defaults.
#
# One file, both consumers: mise.toml loads it via `_.file` for the host
# tooling (`just sync`, `just auth`) and compose.yaml loads it as a layer
# for the container. That is the point — two copies of a credential drift,
# and the one that drifts is discovered at the worst moment.
#
# Keep it to secrets. Non-secret tunables belong in .env.defaults or
# .env.<env> (container) and mise.toml or mise.<env>.toml (host); mise and
# Compose do not resolve precedence identically for everything, and
# secrets-only is what makes that difference impossible to trip over.
#
# Capture DIFMSYNC_API_KEY / DIFMSYNC_MEMBER_ID per docs/difm-api.md.
# DIFMSYNC_API_KEY is long-lived and has no rotation path — treat it as a
# shared-fate secret. No DI.fm password is needed at any point.
DIFMSYNC_API_KEY=
DIFMSYNC_MEMBER_ID=
DIFMSYNC_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
DIFMSYNC_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=
DIFMSYNC_PLAYLIST_ID=

# Only if you registered something other than the default on the Spotify
# app. Must match a registered redirect URI exactly; both the `auth`
# listener's port and its path are derived from it.
# DIFMSYNC_SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback

# Do NOT set DIFMSYNC_AUTH_BIND or DIFMSYNC_DB_PATH here. compose.yaml
# pins both, and a value in this file would be ignored — see the comments
# there for why they are not tunable inside the container.
